{
  "duration": 62.659,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.119,
      "end": 0.28,
      "text": "So"
    },
    {
      "start": 0.819,
      "end": 1.779,
      "text": "welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 2.559,
      "end": 3.98,
      "text": "It's time to solve one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.46,
      "end": 5.139,
      "text": "Now, in this problem,"
    },
    {
      "start": 5.619,
      "end": 8.219,
      "text": "we are given that two trains are moving in the same direction."
    },
    {
      "start": 8.8,
      "end": 10.199,
      "text": "The speed of the first train is"
    },
    {
      "start": 10.679,
      "end": 12.059,
      "text": "seventy kilometers per hour,"
    },
    {
      "start": 12.639,
      "end": 15.939,
      "text": "and the speed of the second train is fifty-two kilometers per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 16.319,
      "end": 20.42,
      "text": "The question is asking us to find their relative speed."
    },
    {
      "start": 20.899,
      "end": 22.18,
      "text": "Now, the important words here are"
    },
    {
      "start": 22.739,
      "end": 23.539,
      "text": "same direction."
    },
    {
      "start": 24.26,
      "end": 25.039,
      "text": "What does this mean?"
    },
    {
      "start": 25.439,
      "end": 29.579,
      "text": "It means both trains are moving one behind the other, so one train is not coming towards the other."
    },
    {
      "start": 29.959,
      "end": 32.779,
      "text": "Instead, one train is only catching up with the other."
    },
    {
      "start": 33.18,
      "end": 34.0,
      "text": "Because of this,"
    },
    {
      "start": 34.479,
      "end": 35.799,
      "text": "we do not add the speeds."
    },
    {
      "start": 36.18,
      "end": 40.619,
      "text": "We always take the difference of their speeds. This is a simple rule to remember."
    },
    {
      "start": 41.02,
      "end": 46.339,
      "text": "If two objects move in the same direction, relative speed equals difference of their speeds. Got it?"
    },
    {
      "start": 46.84,
      "end": 54.739,
      "text": "Perfect. Now let us put the given values. Relative speed equals seventy minus fifty-two. After subtracting, we get eighteen kilometers per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 55.559,
      "end": 55.999,
      "text": "Hence,"
    },
    {
      "start": 56.379,
      "end": 60.459,
      "text": "the relative speed of the two trains is eighteen kilometer per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 60.899,
      "end": 62.659,
      "text": "So the final answer will be option C."
    }
  ],
